WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.213
How to proceed comes down to order.

2
00:00:02.213 --> 00:00:06.650
Order decides whether branch
modernization is a gain or a regression.

3
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.575
First, secure the governor.

4
00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:12.609
The SD-WAN controller is internet-facing
with estate-wide authority,

5
00:00:12.609 --> 00:00:15.228
so it comes under
vulnerability management,

6
00:00:15.228 --> 00:00:19.050
privileged access and off-box
logging before it carries traffic.

7
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.262
Then buy the pipe on measured physics.

8
00:00:21.262 --> 00:00:24.282
Deploy the governor before
production traffic:

9
00:00:24.282 --> 00:00:28.887
a site whose control layer isn't live
and logging doesn't get its new egress.

10
00:00:28.887 --> 00:00:32.400
Treat the boundary change as
the significant change it is,

11
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.449
decided before the first cutover.

12
00:00:34.449 --> 00:00:38.963
And confirm CISA telemetry parity
before any legacy circuit ends.

13
00:00:38.963 --> 00:00:43.137
The book is candid that no memo
or directive sets this sequence.

14
00:00:43.137 --> 00:00:47.988
It's an engineering dependency, and saying
so is what makes it survive review.

15
00:00:47.988 --> 00:00:51.971
Lighting up fast circuits before
the security layer is live is,

16
00:00:51.971 --> 00:00:56.262
in the program's experience, the
most common and most costly mistake.

17
00:00:56.262 --> 00:01:00.038
When funding becomes possible,
prove the case in your own estate.

18
00:01:00.038 --> 00:01:05.613
Instrument two comparable branches for 30
days, change one, and measure 30 more.

19
00:01:05.613 --> 00:01:08.699
That's an effect size a
budget examiner will accept.

20
00:01:08.699 --> 00:01:11.292
The decision: adopt this order as program

21
00:01:11.292 --> 00:01:14.112
policy before the first
production cutover.

22
00:01:14.112 --> 00:01:16.060
Finally, what can start now.
